    "summary": "High‑energy UCSB show with monster Playing In The Band jam",
    "blurb": "The third set delivers a soaring 19‑minute Playing In The Band that erupts into Other One and Eyes Of The World. Earlier sets feature tight rhythm work, a standout Here Comes Sunshine, and seamless China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider transitions. Overall the performance is vibrant despite Garcia’s cold‑strained vocals.",
    "review": "May 20, 1973 at the UC Santa Barbara stadium finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. The first set builds solid momentum with crisp renditions of Bertha, Box of Rain and a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider that sets the tone for the evening. The second set swings through classics like Here Comes Sunshine and Jack Straw before the band launches into an unforgettable third set: Truckin' tears open the floor, spilling into a sprawling Nobody's Fault But Mine Jam, a thunderous jam, then into a 19‑minute Playing In The Band that blossoms into a fiery Other One and a soaring Eyes Of The World, before winding down with Stella Blue and Sugar Magnolia. Jerry’s voice is hoarse from a cold but his guitar work remains incisive; Phil’s bass pumps the jams, Keith’s keyboards add texture, and Bill drives the rhythm with relentless energy. The show captures the band at a creative peak in ’73, offering both tight songcraft and expansive improvisation.",
